    <UnitTestResult executionId="a96d0319-3975-491b-b9d7-31d1ab2df6a8" testId="a99fbd6f-f11a-bda4-1f12-e0c02b836905" testName="WebApi.Tests.Events.EventsTenantIsolationSweepTests.Another_stores_run_sheet_is_never_served_and_never_regenerated" computerName="svens-macbook-pro" duration="00:00:00.0626618" startTime="2026-08-02T10:21:31.2492350+02:00" endTime="2026-08-02T10:21:31.2492350+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="a96d0319-3975-491b-b9d7-31d1ab2df6a8" />
    <UnitTestResult executionId="45dbdbd4-2083-446e-9dd1-ee9d14376b59" testId="309d368e-ccdc-a7a8-947c-15d0c844a398" testName="WebApi.Tests.Events.EventsDepositRailJourneyGapTests.The_Dintero_deposit_rail_is_a_declared_gap_not_a_port_omission" computerName="svens-macbook-pro" duration="00:00:00.0010000" startTime="2026-08-02T10:21:31.5779660+02:00" endTime="2026-08-02T10:21:31.5779660+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="NotExecuted" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="45dbdbd4-2083-446e-9dd1-ee9d14376b59">
      <Output>
        <StdOut>JOURNEY-GAP (Dintero): the guest-facing half EXISTS — a provider-hosted redirect URL, the same ProviderRedirectUrl field the working Vipps rail returns — and so does an inbound completion route (GET /dintero/callback). Three pieces are missing. (1) CREATION: IDinteroService.InitiatePayment re-loads the cart by USER+store (DinteroService.cs:192) and builds the entire order body from it, so a deposit cannot reach it even carrying a cart id; a cartless session-create call would be new provider-integration surface, which the spec excludes (40-events-spec.md:52). (2) CALLBACK RESOLUTION: /dintero/callback parses merchant_reference as a PaymentTransactionId and answers 500 when no such row exists (DinteroController.cs:237-241 -&gt; :304-308) — a deposit writes no PaymentTransaction, so every delivery would 500 and Dintero would retry it indefinitely. (3) MONEY ROUTING, the real blocker and a Sven decision, not an implementation detail: Dintero splits are per ORDER ITEM and computed from the cart, a deposit has no line to split, and there is no stated policy on whether Okam takes commission on an event deposit. Omitting splits pays the venue only where the store holds its OWN Dintero credentials (DinteroFeeCalculationService.cs:112-116); on the platform account the guest's deposit would settle to Okam's payout destination instead of the venue's. Half-wiring this moves real money to the wrong party.</StdOut>
      </Output>
