    <UnitTestResult executionId="dc29664d-e013-4f53-a5ab-e462c53e095b" testId="f9dcf349-c591-3d16-aacf-3d81159aba3a" testName="WebApi.Tests.Events.EventsStateMachineTests.Legal_edge_resolves_to_the_spec_target(transitionId: &quot;T14&quot;, from: Accepted, expected: Cancelled)" computerName="svens-macbook-pro" duration="00:00:00.0000020" startTime="2026-08-02T10:21:21.1399850+02:00" endTime="2026-08-02T10:21:21.1399850+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="dc29664d-e013-4f53-a5ab-e462c53e095b" />
    <UnitTestResult executionId="e9991ed6-c949-43dc-b853-e785e9b925a0" testId="4aa44017-ee65-0ad7-71a5-b0dfafc5391c" testName="WebApi.Tests.Events.EventsDepositRailJourneyGapTests.The_Stripe_deposit_rail_is_a_declared_gap_not_a_port_omission" computerName="svens-macbook-pro" duration="00:00:00.0010000" startTime="2026-08-02T10:21:31.5786370+02:00" endTime="2026-08-02T10:21:31.5786370+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="NotExecuted" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="e9991ed6-c949-43dc-b853-e785e9b925a0">
      <Output>
        <StdOut>JOURNEY-GAP (Stripe): unbuilt at BOTH ends, and three of the four missing pieces are not backend work. CREATION — IStripeService.CreatePaymentIntent requires a cart or giftcard (StripeService.cs:170-172), an authenticated user for the Stripe customer (:192-193) and an already-attached PaymentMethodId with Confirm=true (:210-211), and writes a PaymentTransaction (:241); an Events deposit has none of those (its page is anonymous, addressed only by PublicToken), so spec 40-events-spec.md:240's 'via the existing CreatePaymentIntent client-confirmation path' is not achievable against that method as written. COMPLETION — this branch has no Stripe webhook route and no webhook-secret setting (StripeSettings carries only PublishableKey/SecretKey), no hosted Stripe page or Checkout Session, and no Stripe capture sweeper (the three IUncapturedOrderSweepers are Dintero, Surfboard, Vipps); checkout completes client-driven via POST /carts/complete, which needs a logged-in user and a cart. GUEST SURFACE — the Okam-hosted Stripe Elements form lives in the frontend repo, so no backend change makes a Stripe deposit payable. Wiring Initiate alone would create deposits nobody could ever pay or complete.</StdOut>
      </Output>
    </UnitTestResult>
