[xUnit.net 00:00:11.63]       JOURNEY-GAP (Stripe): unbuilt at BOTH ends, and three of the four missing pieces are not backend work. CREATION — IStripeService.CreatePaymentIntent requires a cart or giftcard (StripeService.cs:170-172), an authenticated user for the Stripe customer (:192-193) and an already-attached PaymentMethodId with Confirm=true (:210-211), and writes a PaymentTransaction (:241); an Events deposit has none of those (its page is anonymous, addressed only by PublicToken), so spec 40-events-spec.md:240's 'via the existing CreatePaymentIntent client-confirmation path' is not achievable against that method as written. COMPLETION — this branch has no Stripe webhook route and no webhook-secret setting (StripeSettings carries only PublishableKey/SecretKey), no hosted Stripe page or Checkout Session, and no Stripe capture sweeper (the three IUncapturedOrderSweepers are Dintero, Surfboard, Vipps); checkout completes client-driven via POST /carts/complete, which needs a logged-in user and a cart. GUEST SURFACE — the Okam-hosted Stripe Elements form lives in the frontend repo, so no backend change makes a Stripe deposit payable. Wiring Initiate alone would create deposits nobody could ever pay or complete.
